# Integration branch

**`integration`** is the merge target for issue work. **`main`** is the release line: it must always **build** and have been **flashed** on hardware before promotion.

## Branch flow

```
fix|feature/<#>-slug  ──PR──►  integration  ──promote──►  main
         ▲                          │
         └── branch from integration ┘
```

## Agents (Cursor Cloud / local)

**May do without asking:**

- Push the issue branch
- Open a PR with base **`integration`** (not `main`)
- Merge that PR into **`integration`** when:
  - Scope is a single issue (`Closes #N`)
  - `./scripts/build.sh` passes (CI green on the PR)
  - No secrets in the diff
  - Clock-face UI: PR notes that hardware QA on **`integration`** is required before promotion (agents cannot flash in cloud)

**Do not** push or merge directly to **`main`**. Promotion only:

```bash
./scripts/promote-integration.sh --flash-ok
```

Run promotion after flashing **`integration`** on a watch and smoke-testing.

## Humans

- Default PR base branch: **`integration`**
- After a batch of merged issue PRs: flash **`integration`**, then run `promote-integration.sh --flash-ok`
- Hotfix on **`main`**: cherry-pick or merge to **`main`**, then merge **`main`** back into **`integration`** so branches do not diverge

See [`docs/WORKFLOW.md`](docs/WORKFLOW.md).
